# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_cochange_persist.py" "COCHANGE PERSIST GATE: PASS" "co-change per-push PERSIST (the increment survives in the store, byte-identical to a batch, moat intact)" "co-change PERSIST: the per-push co-change increment, PERSISTED to the per-tenant store, end to end against a REAL ephemeral Postgres. #259 proved the increment is byte-identical to a batch over the same commits but did NOT persist it -- the co_change store only had a full DELETE+reINSERT writer + a path-FILTERED partner read (no read-back-ALL surface, no n_total column), so the increment could neither recover the seed counters nor merge onto them. This gate proves the persistence: a NEW read-back-all surface (co_change_all_with_authority -> the whole stored pair set in seed_counters shape) + an n_total column (the base-rate N the increment must recover), then the push path reads back -> folds this push's commits via the SHARED fold_commits/emit_pairs (NO clone -- a push payload's commits[] ARE the content-free input) -> re-ingests the merged set through the SAME gated writer, all OFF the event worker (the populate_cochange_async pattern). MEASURE-FIRST: (a) the push increment PERSISTS + survives a re-read (co/n_a/n_b/n_total intact); (b) two pushes folded one-after-another through the persisted seed == ONE batch over the same commits (BYTE-IDENTICAL, tenant-pinned -- the #259 invariant carried through the STORE); (c) SHA-DEDUPE -- a re-delivered push is a true NO-OP (no double-count), and without dedupe it WOULD double-count (so the dispatcher's sha-dedupe is load-bearing); (d) FAIL-OPEN -- an injected error (unresolvable account, malformed payload) returns content-free and NEVER raises (advisory 2nd signal: a failure must not drop the structural verdict), and the unresolved-account case fails CLOSED on the WRITE (no cross-tenant); (e) GOVERNED-WRITE / RLS INTACT -- a NON-App raw INSERT is refused by the forgery gate (the ONLY write path is the gated fn), a 2nd tenant reading the same repo sees NOTHING (FORCE RLS), and the read-back-all surface is content-free (paths + counts only). ADDITIVE migration (new column + new surface, idempotent; apply-to-prod is PO-gated)" "co-change persist: the per-push increment lands in the per-tenant store via a new read-back-all surface + an n_total column, folds byte-identically to a batch (tenant-pinned), sha-deduped, fail-open, and the governed-write + FORCE-RLS moat is intact (forgery gate refuses a non-App write, cross-tenant read sees nothing); content-free" 24
